================================================================================
OTHER UPSTREAM SOURCES
================================================================================

  SLATEC (public domain, no derivative obligation) is a permitted source where
  GSL lacks a routine — e.g. CSEVL/DCSEVL and INITS/INITDS.

  GNU Octave (GPL-3.0-or-later) is a secondary source, but its special
  functions are largely SLATEC-derived (liboctave/external/slatec-fn/); for
  those, port from SLATEC directly rather than inheriting Octave's chain. Only
  genuinely Octave-original routines should be taken from Octave. Neither is
  vendored at present.

